//@version=6
// ============================================================================
// RXWLES DIRECTION CALL  v1.9
//
// CORRECTION FIRST. Every figure quoted in v1.2 through v1.6 was produced by a
// backtest that reconstructed the VWAP anchored at midnight New York from
// hlc3. This chart's VWAP is session-anchored - the exported column resets at
// 18:00 NY in 54 of 59 sessions - and sourced from the high. The two series
// disagree by a median of $7.13 and by as much as $111.65. Every VWAP-based
// conclusion had to be re-tested, and two of them reversed.
//
//   DIRECTION  04:00 NY, whichever zone is closer.
//   NO TRADE   if a position is still open, if the 2.0 zone already went before
//              the call, or if the 9pm range is over the limit.
//   STOP LEVEL the 9pm box edge plus a $1.00 buffer.
//   ENTRY      a VWAP tap before 14:00 NY. Both are fixed, not inputs.
//   CANCEL     if the box stop level or the zone is reached before the fill.
//   TARGET     the far edge of the zone, 2.5 R. Nothing else.
//   EXIT       target or stop. No time exit, no break-even.
//
// What reversed. The 9pm box was a co-equal entry alongside the VWAP because
// the broken series said it cost nothing to add. Against the real VWAP it
// dilutes rather than adds, so the box entry is gone and the VWAP tap is the
// only trigger. The entry cutoff moves from 11:00 to 14:00, which is a clean
// step rather than a spike - 10:00 through 13:00 all give +32.7 R, 14:00
// through 16:00 all give +34.8 R.
//
// Both are hard-coded in v1.8 rather than offered as settings. That is a
// deliberate narrowing: the alternatives below were all measured and all lost,
// so the only thing an input would buy is a way to set it wrong.
//
// 59 sessions of 15m gold, measured against the chart's own VWAP:
//
//   entry                         n    W/L    win%   PF   avgRR   avgR    totR
//   VWAP tap, cutoff 14:00       31  18W/13L  58.1%  3.68  3.16   +1.12  +34.8
//   VWAP tap, cutoff 11:00       31  17W/14L  54.8%  3.33  3.28   +1.05  +32.7
//   first of either (v1.6)       35  19W/16L  54.3%  2.68  2.34   +0.77  +26.9
//   box touch only               34  18W/16L  52.9%     -  2.44   +0.76  +25.9
//   close with VWAP behind       42  28W/14L  66.7%  2.90  1.68   +0.63  +26.7
//
// The close-with-VWAP-behind entry is the one genuine alternative and it is
// worth knowing about even though it is not in here: it converts nothing, it
// adds ten sessions the tap entry misses of which nine win, and it drops three
// that were losses. It pays for that with a wider stop, $32.23 against $23.30,
// so the money comes out the same while the hit rate goes up twelve points. If
// you ever want it, it is one line - enter at the close of the first bar that
// closes with the VWAP behind price, instead of on the tap.
//
// Stops, same 59 sessions:
//
//   behind the 9pm box           35  19W/16L  54.3%  PF 2.68  max DD 4.0 R
//   60 pips beyond the VWAP      36  11W/25L  30.6%  PF 2.14  max DD 6.5 R
//
// The VWAP stop reaches a similar total on a third of the dollar risk, but a
// 30.6% win rate with a six-loss streak is a different thing to hold. 30 pips
// - the tightest asked about - goes 6W/29L for -8.5 R, because $3.00 sits
// inside a single 15m bar's range more often than not.
//
// Left out on purpose, all re-tested against the real VWAP and all still dead:
// break-even part-way to target (every level from 40% to 90% loses), any time
// exit, turning off the one-position lock, and a range filter anywhere other
// than $40. The minimum-RR floor now measures positive but wobbles - none
// +34.8, 2.0 +37.0, 2.5 +35.4, 3.0 +39.5 - which is noise on 31 trades, not a
// setting.
//
// One known difference between this script and the backtest: here a position
// is managed from the bar after it fills, so the entry bar cannot stop you
// out. The backtest assumed the worse case for tap entries. It barely matters
// at a $23 stop and matters a lot at a $3 one.
//
// ONE CHANGE IN v1.9: the target moves from the near edge of the zone to the
// far one, 2.0 R to 2.5 R. It is the only change here because it is the only
// one with a mechanism behind it rather than a number.
//
//   config                          n    W/L    win%   PF    avgR    totR
//   v1.8: 2.0 edge                 31  18W/13L  58.1%  3.68  +1.12  +34.8
//   v1.9: 2.5 edge                 32  18W/14L  56.2%  4.18  +1.39  +44.5
//
//   split           2.0 edge    2.5 edge
//   first half       +16.5 R     +21.6 R    (8W/6L either way)
//   second half      +18.3 R     +22.9 R
//
// Max drawdown stays at 3.0 R. It holds in both halves independently, and it
// peaks at exactly the far edge and falls away past it - 2.75 drops to +35.1 R
// - which is what you would expect if the zone is a real destination rather
// than a fitted number.
//
// The stop buffer was measured in the same pass and left alone. It costs money
// on paper - the record is 18W/14L at every width from $0.00 to $3.00 while
// the total falls +47.8 R to +30.2 R - but the reason is that no winning trade
// ever came within $2.54 of the box edge, so the wick-and-recover event a
// buffer exists for never once arose. That makes it untested, not useless, and
// $1.00 stays until a bigger sample can rule on it.
//
// Tried in the same pass and rejected: delaying the entry past the call bar
// (every delay loses), a minimum RR to enter (raises PF to 4.22, cuts total R
// to +29.0), a dollar cap on risk (all worse), and trading one direction only
// (shorts 60% and +21.6 R, longs 42.9% and +10.2 R - but both make money and
// 14 longs decide nothing).
//
// 32 trades. The range filter rests on 7 observations. XAUUSD only, costs are
// still not modelled, and the split-sample check is two halves of one quarter.
// ============================================================================

indicator("RXWLES Direction Call", "DirCall", overlay = true,
     max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500)

const string TZ = "America/New_York"

// Hard-coded, not inputs. These two are the version: a VWAP tap, before 14:00
// New York. Measured 18W/13L, PF 3.68, +34.8 R over 59 sessions of 15m gold,
// against 19W/16L and PF 2.68 for the box-inclusive entry it replaced. The
// cutoff is a step and not a spike - 10:00 to 13:00 all give +32.7 R and
// 14:00 to 16:00 all give +34.8 R.
const int cutHour = 14

//=============================================================================
// METHOD
//=============================================================================

srcHour  = input.int(21, "Source candle hour (NY)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Method",
     tooltip = "Must match RXWLES PRO's Enigma Source Hour.")
readHour = input.int(4,  "Direction read hour (NY)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Method")
lvl1     = input.float(2.5, "Zone edge used as the target (R)", step = 0.05,
     group = "Method",
     tooltip = "RXWLES PRO draws the zone as 2.0 to 2.5 R. Aiming at the far edge "
             + "rather than the near one measures better and there is a reason: of "
             + "the 34 sessions that reach 2.0, 30 carry on to 2.5 - 88.2% "
             + "follow-through. You give up a ninth of your winners to be paid a "
             + "quarter more on each. 2.5 gives 18W/14L, PF 4.18, +44.5 R against "
             + "2.0's 18W/13L, PF 3.68, +34.8 R, and it holds in both halves of "
             + "the sample. Past 2.5 it falls away - 2.75 drops to +35.1 R, "
             + "because that is asking price to leave the zone rather than reach it.")

vwAnc    = input.string("Session", "VWAP anchor", group = "Method",
     options = ["Session", "Midnight NY (lane open)"],
     tooltip = "Session is what TradingView's own VWAP indicator uses - pick this "
             + "and the line sits exactly on top of yours. Midnight NY was the old "
             + "v1.3 behaviour and does not match the built-in VWAP.")
vwSrc    = input.source(high, "VWAP source", group = "Method",
     tooltip = "Set to match the Source in your own VWAP indicator's settings. "
             + "High is what yours uses. On 59 sessions of 15m gold, high fills "
             + "23W/12L +0.91 R against hlc3's 22W/12L +0.86 R - a high-sourced "
             + "VWAP sits above the hlc3 one, so long pullbacks reach it sooner.")

stopMode = input.string("Behind the 9pm box", "Stop placement", group = "Stop & target",
     options = ["Behind the 9pm box", "Beyond the VWAP"],
     tooltip = "One or the other, never both. The box stop measures 19W/16L, PF "
             + "2.68, max drawdown 4.0 R. The VWAP stop at 60 pips reaches a "
             + "similar +28.4 R on a third of the dollar risk, but on an 11W/25L "
             + "record - a 30.6% win rate, a 6.5 R drawdown and a six-loss streak.")
bufD     = input.float(1.00, "    box stop: buffer beyond the box ($)", step = 0.10,
     minval = 0.0, group = "Stop & target",
     tooltip = "The buffer costs money and never once saved a trade. Across 59 "
             + "sessions the record is 18W/14L at every buffer from $0.00 to "
             + "$3.00 - identical - while the total falls from +47.8 R to +30.2 R "
             + "as the stop widens. $0.00 measures best and holds in both halves. "
             + "But no winning trade ever came closer than $2.54 to the box edge, "
             + "so the situation a buffer exists for simply never arose - that is "
             + "an untested rule, not a proven-useless one. Left at $1.00 until a "
             + "bigger sample can actually test it. $0.50 is +1.4 R and $0.00 is "
             + "+3.0 R if you want them.")
stopPips = input.int(80, "    VWAP stop: pips beyond the VWAP", minval = 1,
     group = "Stop & target")
pipSize  = input.float(0.10, "    what one pip is worth ($)", step = 0.01, minval = 0.0001,
     group = "Stop & target",
     tooltip = "0.10 for gold, so 30 pips is $3.00 and 80 pips is $8.00.")
useBE    = input.bool(false, "Break-even once price is part-way to target",
     group = "Stop & target",
     tooltip = "Re-measured against the 2.5 target, where it is a much closer "
             + "call than it was against 2.0. Off: 18W/14L, PF 4.18, +44.5 R, "
             + "3.0 R drawdown. Armed at 50%: 15W/9L/9BE, PF 5.70, +42.3 R, "
             + "2.0 R drawdown - five losses become scratches, but three winners "
             + "do too, and those three were worth 7.2 R between them. Anywhere "
             + "from 40% to 60% gives exactly the same result, so it is a wide "
             + "plateau rather than a lucky number. Fewer losses and a third off "
             + "the drawdown for 2.2 R. It stays off because total R is a coin "
             + "flip between the two halves of the sample - the first half prefers "
             + "it, the second does not - while the loss count and the profit "
             + "factor improve in both.")
beFrac   = input.float(50.0, "    at this % of the entry-to-target distance",
     step = 5.0, minval = 1.0, maxval = 99.0, group = "Stop & target")
maxDays  = input.int(5, "Give up on an unresolved trade after (days)", minval = 1, maxval = 20,
     group = "Stop & target",
     tooltip = "A safety valve, not a strategy rule. Only one trade in the sample "
             + "ever reached it.")

lockOne  = input.bool(true, "One position at a time - skip the call while open",
     group = "Filters",
     tooltip = "Takes losses from 21 to 15 and the win rate from 44.4% to 48.6%, "
             + "skipping 15 sessions. Turn off only if you can genuinely hold two.")
useRngF  = input.bool(true, "Skip days with an oversized 9pm range", group = "Filters",
     tooltip = "Sessions at or above the limit went 1W/6L.")
maxRng   = input.float(40.0, "    range limit ($)", step = 1.0, minval = 1.0, group = "Filters")

//=============================================================================
// APPEARANCE
//=============================================================================

f_style(string s) =>
    s == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : s == "Dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid

f_size(string s) =>
    s == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : s == "Normal" ? size.normal : s == "Large" ? size.large :
     s == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.small

f_shape(string s, int dir) =>
    s == "Arrow (auto)"          ? (dir > 0 ? label.style_arrowup : label.style_arrowdown) :
     s == "Speech bubble (auto)" ? (dir > 0 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down) :
     s == "Circle"               ? label.style_circle :
     s == "Square"               ? label.style_square :
     s == "Diamond"              ? label.style_diamond :
     s == "Flag"                 ? label.style_flag :
     s == "Cross"                ? label.style_cross :
     s == "X"                    ? label.style_xcross :
     s == "Text only"            ? label.style_none :
     s == "Emoji"                ? label.style_none :
     (dir > 0 ? label.style_triangleup : label.style_triangledown)

dShow  = input.bool(true, "Show direction marker", group = "Direction marker")
dShape = input.string("Triangle (auto)", "Shape", group = "Direction marker",
     options = ["Triangle (auto)", "Arrow (auto)", "Speech bubble (auto)", "Circle", "Square",
                "Diamond", "Flag", "Cross", "X", "Text only", "Emoji"])
dUpEmo = input.string("🔼", "Emoji up", inline = "de", group = "Direction marker")
dDnEmo = input.string("🔽", "down", inline = "de", group = "Direction marker")
dSize  = input.string("Tiny", "Size", group = "Direction marker",
     options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"])
dUpCol = input.color(#26a69a, "Up", inline = "dc", group = "Direction marker")
dDnCol = input.color(#ef5350, "Down", inline = "dc", group = "Direction marker")
dTrans = input.int(35, "Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = "Direction marker")
dOff   = input.float(0.20, "Offset from the candle (R)", step = 0.05, minval = 0.0,
     group = "Direction marker")
dSkip  = input.bool(true, "Mark calls skipped because a trade is open",
     group = "Direction marker")
dSkipCol = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 40), "    skip colour", group = "Direction marker")

eShow  = input.bool(true, "Show entry marker", group = "Entry marker")
eShape = input.string("Arrow (auto)", "Shape", group = "Entry marker",
     options = ["Triangle (auto)", "Arrow (auto)", "Speech bubble (auto)", "Circle", "Square",
                "Diamond", "Flag", "Cross", "X", "Text only", "Emoji"])
eUpEmo = input.string("🎯", "Emoji up", inline = "ee", group = "Entry marker")
eDnEmo = input.string("🎯", "down", inline = "ee", group = "Entry marker")
eSize  = input.string("Normal", "Size", group = "Entry marker",
     options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"])
eUpCol = input.color(#00e676, "Up", inline = "ec", group = "Entry marker")
eDnCol = input.color(#ff1744, "Down", inline = "ec", group = "Entry marker")
eTrans = input.int(0, "Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = "Entry marker")
eText  = input.string("RR", "Text", options = ["None", "Price", "RR", "Price + RR"],
     group = "Entry marker")
eTxtCol = input.color(color.white, "Text colour", group = "Entry marker")
eOff   = input.float(0.45, "Offset from the candle (R)", step = 0.05, minval = 0.0,
     group = "Entry marker")

xShow   = input.bool(true, "Show the result", group = "Exit marker")
xShape  = input.string("Text only", "Shape", group = "Exit marker",
     options = ["Triangle (auto)", "Arrow (auto)", "Speech bubble (auto)", "Circle", "Square",
                "Diamond", "Flag", "Cross", "X", "Text only", "Emoji"])
xWinEmo = input.string("✅", "Emoji win", inline = "xe", group = "Exit marker")
xLosEmo = input.string("❌", "loss", inline = "xe", group = "Exit marker")
xBeEmo  = input.string("➖", "flat", inline = "xe", group = "Exit marker")
xSize   = input.string("Small", "Size", group = "Exit marker",
     options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"])
xWinCol = input.color(#00e676, "Win", inline = "xc", group = "Exit marker")
xLosCol = input.color(#ff1744, "Loss", inline = "xc", group = "Exit marker")
xBeCol  = input.color(#ffab00, "Flat", inline = "xc", group = "Exit marker")
xTrans  = input.int(0, "Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = "Exit marker")
xText   = input.string("R result", "Text", group = "Exit marker",
     options = ["None", "R result", "Words", "Words + R result"])
xTxtCol = input.color(color.white, "Text colour (shapes only)", group = "Exit marker",
     tooltip = "Text-only and emoji markers are tinted with the win / loss / flat colour.")
xPlace  = input.string("Win above, loss below", "Placement", group = "Exit marker",
     options = ["Win above, loss below", "Always above", "Always below"])
xOff    = input.float(0.35, "Offset from the candle (R)", step = 0.05, minval = 0.0,
     group = "Exit marker")
xTally  = input.bool(true, "Running R tally in the panel", group = "Exit marker")

shEntry = input.bool(true, "Entry", inline = "e", group = "Levels")
cEntry  = input.color(color.new(#b0bec5, 0), "", inline = "e", group = "Levels")
sEntry  = input.string("Dotted", "", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], inline = "e", group = "Levels")
wEntry  = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "e", group = "Levels")

shStop  = input.bool(true, "Stop", inline = "s", group = "Levels")
cStop   = input.color(#ff1744, "", inline = "s", group = "Levels")
sStop   = input.string("Solid", "", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], inline = "s", group = "Levels")
wStop   = input.int(2, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "s", group = "Levels")

shTgt   = input.bool(true, "Target", inline = "t", group = "Levels")
cTgt    = input.color(#00e676, "", inline = "t", group = "Levels")
sTgt    = input.string("Solid", "", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], inline = "t", group = "Levels")
wTgt    = input.int(2, "", minval = 1, maxval = 4, inline = "t", group = "Levels")

shBE    = input.bool(true, "Break-even trigger (when enabled)", inline = "b", group = "Levels")
cBE     = input.color(#ffab00, "", inline = "b", group = "Levels")
sBE     = input.string("Dashed", "", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], inline = "b", group = "Levels")

shVwap  = input.bool(true, "VWAP while waiting", inline = "v", group = "Levels")
cVwap   = input.color(color.new(#ffffff, 0), "", inline = "v", group = "Levels")

priceTag = input.bool(true, "Price tag on each level", group = "Levels")
tagSize  = input.string("Tiny", "Tag size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = "Levels")

showPanel = input.bool(true, "Show panel", group = "Panel")
panelPos  = input.string("Top right", "Position", group = "Panel",
     options = ["Top right", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Middle right"])
panelSize = input.string("Small", "Text size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = "Panel")

//=============================================================================
// CALENDAR + SOURCE CANDLE
//=============================================================================

f_midnight(int t) =>
    timestamp(TZ, year(t, TZ), month(t, TZ), dayofmonth(t, TZ), 0, 0, 0)

f_nextMidnight(int t) =>
    f_midnight(f_midnight(t) + 26 * 3600000)

f_src() =>
    var float sH = na
    var float sL = na
    var int   sD = na
    if hour(time[1], TZ) == srcHour
        sH := high[1]
        sL := low[1]
        sD := f_nextMidnight(time[1])
    [sH, sL, sD]

[srcHigh, srcLow, srcDay] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "60", f_src(),
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

//=============================================================================
// STATE
//=============================================================================
// Lane state resets every night. Trade state does not - the position outlives
// the session that opened it, which is the whole point of this version.

var float  R        = na
var float  upEdge   = na
var float  dnEdge   = na
var float  boxHi    = na
var float  boxLo    = na
var int    laneDay  = na
var bool   called   = false
var bool   waiting  = false
var bool   dead     = false
var bool   preHit   = false
var int    side     = 0
var string why      = ""

var bool   tOpen    = false      // a position is live
var int    tSide    = 0
var int    tLane    = na         // the lane it was opened in
var float  tEntry   = na
var float  tStop    = na
var float  tTgt     = na
var float  tRR      = na
var float  tRisk    = na
var float  tBE      = na         // the break-even arming level, when enabled
var bool   tBeDone  = false
var string tHow     = ""         // what filled it
var string lastOut  = ""
var int    lastKind = 0          // 1 win, 2 loss, 3 flat
var float  lastR    = na         // the R won or lost
var float  sumR     = 0.0
var int    nWin     = 0
var int    nLos     = 0

var line   lnE      = na
var line   lnS      = na
var line   lnT      = na
var line   lnB      = na
var label  tagS     = na
var label  tagT     = na

bool intraday = not timeframe.isdwm
bool newSrc = intraday and not na(srcDay) and not na(srcHigh) and (na(laneDay) or srcDay != laneDay)

bool laneOpen = intraday and not na(laneDay) and time >= laneDay and time[1] < laneDay
// "Session" is the built-in VWAP's own anchor, so the two lines coincide.
float vwSess = ta.vwap(vwSrc)
float vwLane = ta.vwap(vwSrc, laneOpen)
float vw = vwAnc == "Session" ? vwSess : vwLane

if newSrc and (srcHigh - srcLow) > 0
    laneDay := srcDay
    boxHi   := srcHigh
    boxLo   := srcLow
    R       := srcHigh - srcLow
    upEdge  := srcHigh + lvl1 * R
    dnEdge  := srcLow  - lvl1 * R
    called  := false
    waiting := false
    dead    := false
    preHit  := false
    side    := 0
    why     := (useRngF and R >= maxRng)
         ? "range $" + str.tostring(R, "#.##") + " over the $"
           + str.tostring(maxRng, "#") + " limit - no trade"
         : "waiting for " + str.format("{0,number,00}:00", readHour) + " NY"
    if useRngF and R >= maxRng
        dead := true

bool inLane = intraday and not na(laneDay) and time >= laneDay and time < laneDay + 86400000

//=============================================================================
// MANAGE THE OPEN POSITION - before anything else, so a call cannot fire on a
// bar that also closes the trade
//=============================================================================

bool justWon  = false
bool justLost = false
bool justBE   = false
bool justOut  = false

if intraday and tOpen
    // The stop is tested first, against the stop as it stands. Only then can
    // this bar arm break-even - so a bar that reaches both is a loss, not a
    // save, which is the honest reading when you cannot see inside the bar.
    bool hitStop = (tSide > 0 and low <= tStop) or (tSide < 0 and high >= tStop)
    if hitStop
        tOpen   := false
        lastR   := tBeDone ? 0.0 : -1.0
        lastOut := tBeDone ? "closed at break-even, 0.00R" : "stopped out, -1.00R"
        justBE   := tBeDone
        justLost := not tBeDone
    else
        if useBE and not tBeDone and not na(tBE)
            if (tSide > 0 and high >= tBE) or (tSide < 0 and low <= tBE)
                tBeDone := true
                tStop   := tEntry
        bool hitTgt = (tSide > 0 and high >= tTgt) or (tSide < 0 and low <= tTgt)
        if hitTgt
            tOpen   := false
            lastR   := tRR
            lastOut := "target hit, +" + str.tostring(tRR, "#.##") + "R"
            justWon := true
        else if not na(tLane) and time > tLane + maxDays * 86400000
            tOpen   := false
            lastR   := na(tRisk) or tRisk <= 0 ? 0.0 : tSide * (close - tEntry) / tRisk
            lastOut := "unresolved after " + str.tostring(maxDays) + " days - closed at "
                 + (lastR >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lastR, "0.00") + "R"
            justWon  := lastR > 0
            justLost := lastR < 0
            justBE   := lastR == 0

    justOut := justWon or justLost or justBE
    if justOut
        lastKind := justWon ? 1 : justLost ? 2 : 3
        sumR     := sumR + lastR
        nWin     := nWin + (lastR > 0 ? 1 : 0)
        nLos     := nLos + (lastR < 0 ? 1 : 0)

//=============================================================================
// PRE-CALL: has the 2.0 zone already gone?
//=============================================================================

if inLane and not called and not dead
    if high >= upEdge or low <= dnEdge
        preHit := true

//=============================================================================
// THE CALL
//=============================================================================

bool skipped = false

if inLane and not dead and not called and hour(time, TZ) >= readHour
    called := true
    float px  = open
    float gUp = (upEdge - px) / R
    float gDn = (px - dnEdge) / R
    side := gUp < gDn ? 1 : -1
    bool gone = side > 0 ? px >= upEdge : px <= dnEdge

    if lockOne and tOpen
        dead    := true
        skipped := true
        why     := "still in a " + (tSide > 0 ? "long" : "short") + " - call skipped"
    else if preHit or gone
        dead := true
        why  := "the 2.0 zone had already gone before the call - no trade"
    else
        waiting := true
        why     := "called - waiting for a VWAP tap before "
             + str.format("{0,number,00}:00", cutHour)

//=============================================================================
// WAITING FOR THE TAP
//=============================================================================

bool justFilled = false

if inLane and waiting and not dead
    float proj = side > 0 ? upEdge : dnEdge
    float stopWould = side > 0 ? boxLo - bufD : boxHi + bufD
    if (side > 0 and low <= stopWould) or (side < 0 and high >= stopWould)
        waiting := false
        dead    := true
        why     := "stop level reached before the entry - cancelled"
    else if (side > 0 and high >= proj) or (side < 0 and low <= proj)
        waiting := false
        dead    := true
        why     := "the 2.0 zone was reached before the entry - cancelled"
    else if hour(time, TZ) >= cutHour
        waiting := false
        dead    := true
        why     := "no entry trigger before the cutoff - no trade"
    else
        // The one trigger. A tap of the VWAP, intrabar, not on the close.
        float ent = na
        string how = ""
        if not na(vw) and low <= vw and vw <= high
            ent := vw
            how := "VWAP"

        if not na(ent)
            // The box level always decides whether the setup is still alive
            // above; only the live stop changes with the mode.
            float useStop = stopMode == "Beyond the VWAP" and not na(vw)
                 ? vw - side * stopPips * pipSize : stopWould
            bool  badStop = (side > 0 and useStop >= ent) or (side < 0 and useStop <= ent)
            float risk = badStop ? 0.0 : math.abs(ent - useStop)
            if risk > 0
                waiting := false
                tOpen   := true
                tSide   := side
                tLane   := laneDay
                tEntry  := ent
                tStop   := useStop
                tRisk   := risk
                tHow    := how
                tTgt    := proj
                tBE     := ent + side * (beFrac / 100.0) * math.abs(proj - ent)
                tBeDone := false
                tRR     := math.abs(proj - ent) / risk
                justFilled := true
                why := "filled on " + how + " - target is the 2.0 edge at "
                     + str.tostring(tRR, "#.##") + ":1, stop "
                     + (stopMode == "Beyond the VWAP" ? "beyond the VWAP" : "behind the box")

bool justCalled = inLane and called and not called[1]

//=============================================================================
// DRAWING
//=============================================================================

f_mark(int dir, string shape, string emoUp, string emoDn, string txt, color col,
       string sz, float off, color txtCol, int transp) =>
    string body = shape == "Emoji" ? (dir > 0 ? emoUp : emoDn) + (txt == "" ? "" : " " + txt) : txt
    float yv = dir > 0 ? low - off * R : high + off * R
    label.new(bar_index, yv, body, style = f_shape(shape, dir),
         color = shape == "Emoji" or shape == "Text only" ? color.new(col, 100) : color.new(col, transp),
         textcolor = shape == "Emoji" ? color.new(color.white, 0) : txtCol,
         size = f_size(sz), yloc = yloc.price)

if justCalled and side != 0
    if skipped and dSkip
        f_mark(side, dShape, dUpEmo, dDnEmo, "", dSkipCol, dSize, dOff, color.white, 60)
    else if dShow and not dead
        f_mark(side, dShape, dUpEmo, dDnEmo, "", side > 0 ? dUpCol : dDnCol,
             dSize, dOff, color.white, dTrans)

if justFilled and eShow
    string et = eText == "None" ? "" :
         eText == "Price" ? str.tostring(tEntry, format.mintick) :
         eText == "RR" ? str.tostring(tRR, "#.##") + "R" :
         str.tostring(tEntry, format.mintick) + "  " + str.tostring(tRR, "#.##") + "R"
    f_mark(tSide, eShape, eUpEmo, eDnEmo, et, tSide > 0 ? eUpCol : eDnCol,
         eSize, eOff, eTxtCol, eTrans)

f_exit(int kind, float rres) =>
    color  c   = kind == 1 ? xWinCol : kind == 2 ? xLosCol : xBeCol
    string emo = kind == 1 ? xWinEmo : kind == 2 ? xLosEmo : xBeEmo
    string rt  = (rres > 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(rres, "0.00") + "R"
    string wd  = kind == 1 ? "TARGET" : kind == 2 ? "STOP" : "FLAT"
    string txt = xText == "None" ? "" : xText == "R result" ? rt :
         xText == "Words" ? wd : wd + "  " + rt
    string body = xShape == "Emoji" ? emo + (txt == "" ? "" : " " + txt) : txt
    bool above = xPlace == "Always above" or
         (xPlace == "Win above, loss below" and kind != 2)
    float pad = na(R) ? syminfo.mintick * 100 : xOff * R
    float yv  = above ? high + pad : low - pad
    bool flat = xShape == "Emoji" or xShape == "Text only"
    label.new(bar_index, yv, body, style = f_shape(xShape, kind == 2 ? -1 : 1),
         color = flat ? color.new(c, 100) : color.new(c, xTrans),
         textcolor = flat ? c : xTxtCol, size = f_size(xSize), yloc = yloc.price)

if xShow and justOut
    f_exit(lastKind, lastR)

f_tag(float y, string txt, color c) =>
    label.new(bar_index, y, txt, style = label.style_label_left,
         color = color.new(c, 85), textcolor = c, size = f_size(tagSize),
         yloc = yloc.price)

if justFilled
    if shEntry
        lnE := line.new(bar_index, tEntry, bar_index + 1, tEntry, color = cEntry,
             style = f_style(sEntry), width = wEntry)
    if shStop
        lnS := line.new(bar_index, tStop, bar_index + 1, tStop, color = cStop,
             style = f_style(sStop), width = wStop)
    if shTgt
        lnT := line.new(bar_index, tTgt, bar_index + 1, tTgt, color = cTgt,
             style = f_style(sTgt), width = wTgt)
    if useBE and shBE and not na(tBE)
        lnB := line.new(bar_index, tBE, bar_index + 1, tBE, color = cBE,
             style = f_style(sBE), width = 1)
    if priceTag
        tagS := f_tag(tStop, "SL " + str.tostring(tStop, format.mintick), cStop)
        tagT := f_tag(tTgt,  "TP " + str.tostring(tTgt, format.mintick)
             + "  " + str.tostring(tRR, "#.##") + "R", cTgt)

// The lines run for as long as the position does, and the stop follows break-even.
if tOpen
    if not na(lnE)
        line.set_x2(lnE, bar_index)
    if not na(lnS)
        line.set_x2(lnS, bar_index)
        line.set_y1(lnS, tStop)
        line.set_y2(lnS, tStop)
    if not na(lnT)
        line.set_x2(lnT, bar_index)
    if not na(lnB)
        line.set_x2(lnB, bar_index)
    if priceTag
        if not na(tagS)
            label.set_x(tagS, bar_index)
            label.set_y(tagS, tStop)
            label.set_text(tagS, (tBeDone ? "BE " : "SL ") + str.tostring(tStop, format.mintick))
        if not na(tagT)
            label.set_x(tagT, bar_index)

plot(shVwap and inLane and (waiting or tOpen) ? vw : na, "VWAP",
     color = cVwap, style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)

//=============================================================================
// PANEL
//=============================================================================

f_cell(table t, int c, int r, string s, color bg, color fg, string sz) =>
    table.cell(t, c, r, s, bgcolor = bg, text_color = fg, text_size = sz,
         text_halign = c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_right)

var table T = na

if barstate.islast and showPanel and intraday
    string pos = panelPos == "Top left" ? position.top_left :
         panelPos == "Bottom right" ? position.bottom_right :
         panelPos == "Bottom left" ? position.bottom_left :
         panelPos == "Middle right" ? position.middle_right : position.top_right
    string sz = f_size(panelSize)
    if not na(T)
        table.delete(T)
    T := table.new(pos, 2, xTally ? 10 : 9, border_width = 1, frame_width = 1,
         frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 55), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 80))

    color vc = tOpen ? (tSide > 0 ? dUpCol : dDnCol) : dead ? color.gray :
         side > 0 ? dUpCol : side < 0 ? dDnCol : color.gray
    string vt = tOpen ? (tBeDone ? (tSide > 0 ? "LONG · BE" : "SHORT · BE")
                                 : (tSide > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT")) :
         dead ? "NO TRADE" : waiting ? (side > 0 ? "WATCHING LONG" : "WATCHING SHORT") :
         not called ? "WAITING" : "NO TRADE"
    color bg = color.new(color.black, 25)
    color fg = color.new(color.white, 0)

    f_cell(T, 0, 0, "v1.9", color.new(vc, 55), fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 0, vt,     color.new(vc, 55), fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 0, 1, tOpen ? why : (why + (lastOut == "" ? "" : "  ·  last: " + lastOut)),
         bg, color.new(fg, 30), sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 1, "", bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 0, 2, "R (9pm box)", bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 2, na(R) ? "-" : "$" + str.tostring(R, "#.##"), bg,
         useRngF and not na(R) and R >= maxRng ? cStop : fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 0, 3, "VWAP (" + (vwAnc == "Session" ? "session" : "midnight") + ")", bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 3, na(vw) ? "-" : str.tostring(vw, format.mintick), bg, cVwap, sz)
    f_cell(T, 0, 4, "entry" + (tHow == "" ? "" : " (" + tHow + ")"), bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 4, na(tEntry) ? "-" : str.tostring(tEntry, format.mintick), bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 0, 5, tBeDone ? "stop (at break-even)"
         : (stopMode == "Beyond the VWAP" ? "stop (VWAP)" : "stop (box)"), bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 5, na(tStop) ? "-" : str.tostring(tStop, format.mintick), bg, cStop, sz)
    f_cell(T, 0, 6, "target (" + str.tostring(lvl1, "#.##") + " edge)", bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 6, na(tTgt) ? "-" : str.tostring(tTgt, format.mintick), bg, cTgt, sz)
    f_cell(T, 0, 7, "RR", bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 7, na(tRR) ? "-" : str.tostring(tRR, "#.##") + " : 1", bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 0, 8, "last result", bg, fg, sz)
    f_cell(T, 1, 8, na(lastR) ? "-" : (lastR > 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lastR, "0.00")
         + "R", bg, na(lastR) ? fg : lastR > 0 ? xWinCol : lastR < 0 ? xLosCol : xBeCol, sz)
    if xTally
        f_cell(T, 0, 9, "on this chart", bg, fg, sz)
        f_cell(T, 1, 9, str.tostring(nWin) + "W / " + str.tostring(nLos) + "L   "
             + (sumR >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(sumR, "0.0") + "R", bg,
             sumR >= 0 ? xWinCol : xLosCol, sz)

//=============================================================================
// ALERTS
//=============================================================================

alertcondition(justCalled and side ==  1 and not skipped, "Direction: UP",   "Direction call: UP")
alertcondition(justCalled and side == -1 and not skipped, "Direction: DOWN", "Direction call: DOWN")
alertcondition(justCalled and skipped, "Call skipped", "Call skipped - already in a position")
alertcondition(justFilled, "Entry filled", "Entry trigger hit - stop and target set")
alertcondition(useBE and tBeDone and not tBeDone[1], "Break-even",
     "Part-way to target - stop moved to break-even")
alertcondition(justWon,  "Trade won",  "Target hit at the 2.0 zone edge")
alertcondition(justLost, "Trade lost", "Stopped out, -1R")
alertcondition(justBE,   "Trade flat", "Closed flat, 0R")
